WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.270
Use a consistent identity model across local services, cloud accounts, gateways, storage, and applications.

00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:12.663
Grant least privilege and require authentication at every exposed endpoint.

00:00:12.663 --> 00:00:24.154
Segment management, model-serving, storage, and user traffic so compromise of a front end does not provide unrestricted access to private data or infrastructure.

00:00:24.154 --> 00:00:30.485
Store provider keys, model tokens, and service credentials in managed secrets systems.

00:00:30.485 --> 00:00:38.224
Rotate them, restrict their scope, and prevent them from entering prompts, images, repositories, or logs.

00:00:38.224 --> 00:00:45.962
Patch local operating systems, GPU drivers, runtimes, gateways, containers, and cloud components through controlled releases.

00:00:45.962 --> 00:00:52.763
Hybrid systems have a larger dependency surface, so version inventory and rollback matter.

00:00:52.763 --> 00:00:59.563
Audit routing decisions, configuration changes, authentication, administrative actions, costs, errors, and security events.

00:00:59.563 --> 00:01:07.302
Minimize sensitive prompt and output content in logs while preserving enough evidence to investigate incidents.

00:01:07.302 --> 00:01:18.792
Correlate local and cloud timestamps and request identifiers so an end-to-end event can be reconstructed without copying private data into every monitoring system.

00:01:18.792 --> 00:01:27.000
Prepare incident procedures for data misrouting, exposed credentials, provider outage, compromised local nodes, and unexpected spending.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:36.145
Define how to disable a route, revoke keys, isolate systems, preserve evidence, restore configuration, and communicate degraded capability.

00:01:36.145 --> 00:01:41.070
Back up irreplaceable data and policy, and test rollback.

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:51.153
Review vendor security, availability, retention, and exit options because provider risk is part of the architecture, not an external footnote.
